MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CI has been red at the `npm run type-check` step: 7 errors across the
build-runs and telemetry API routes.

Two stale generated files, both additive to fix:

1. src/routeTree.gen.ts had not been regenerated after PR #14 added
   /api/build-runs/$id/{cancel,events} and /api/telemetry/client, so
   createFileRoute() rejected all three paths as absent from
   FileRoutesByPath. Regenerated by the TanStack Start plugin via
   `npm run build` (63 insertions, no deletions).

2. src/types/database.generated.ts was missing ten tables that already
   exist in the live database, so `.from("build_runs")` and friends
   resolved to `never`. Added build_run_events, build_run_steps,
   build_runs, client_telemetry, controlled_template_versions,
   generation_files, generation_runs, job_executions, project_revisions
   and repair_outcomes, rendered with the repo's own generator logic
   from the live schema so a future `npm run generate:database-types`
   reproduces them byte for byte.

With real types in place, the `as any` on the repair_outcomes insert is
no longer needed and is removed. The casts on client_telemetry and
build_run_events inserts are kept and now carry a comment: their `id` is
GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, which PostgREST still reports as required,
so the generated Insert type demands an id the database refuses.

type-check 0 errors, 622/622 tests pass, lint 0 errors, build succeeds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QGy3NZWndBAVM8qKdAzXm1
